---
import Fastfetch from "@/components/sections/about/Fastfetch.astro";
import SkillsGrid from "@/components/sections/about/SkillsGrid.astro";
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About">
  <section class="flex flex-col gap-16 min-h-svh" aria-label="About">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-4.5">
      <h1 class="text-3xl leading-tight tracking-tight font-600">About</h1>
      <p class="color-portfolio-muted leading-relaxed max-w-prose">
        I'm Julian Peter Gerona, JP. I'm a 4th year Information Technology
        student at Mapúa Malayan Colleges Laguna, specializing in
        cybersecurity, graduating in 2026. I build web and mobile software:
        interfaces in React and Astro, APIs in Express and Django, native
        Android in Kotlin with Jetpack Compose.
      </p>
      <p class="color-portfolio-muted leading-relaxed max-w-prose">
        I use AI heavily when I build, and I don't pretend otherwise. What
        keeps the output worth shipping is the software engineering behind it:
        I decide the architecture, review every line the way I review my own,
        and throw away what doesn't hold up.
      </p>
      <p class="color-portfolio-muted leading-relaxed max-w-prose">
        I work by kaizen, continuous small improvements. This site is on its
        second rebuild, and the project write-ups here record what I got wrong
        before what worked.
      </p>
    </div>

    <SkillsGrid />

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-4.5">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-1.5">
        <h2 class="text-[1.375rem] leading-tight font-400 font-serif">Setup</h2>
        <p class="text-sm color-portfolio-muted leading-snug max-w-prose">
          Every project on this site was built on a 13-inch early-2015
          MacBook Air. It's slow, and it keeps me honest about performance.
        </p>
      </div>
      <Fastfetch />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
